{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar","id":968127,"title":"Conan the Solar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T13:55:36-07:00","id":968127,"title":"Conan the Solar","content":"Conan the Cimmerian is cited as inspiration for <b>Exalted</b>. To quote the book: \u201cSolars owe a lot of their DNA to Conan, an ostensibly mortal man who yet demonstrates superhuman might, quickness, and resistance to injury.\u201d I agree with the assessment, but whether Conan himself is a Solar is an interesting question. Most of his abilities are within mortal bounds, which is what makes him so interesting. The following is a tour of Conan\u2019s abilities, and where I believe he needs to step beyond mortal bounds into the realm of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> First, let\u2019s talk about Conan\u2019s strength. The man can throw a bench made of silver. He can yank out crucifix nails driven into his own legs. He\u2019s <i>strong</i>! But\u2026 is he supernaturally strong? It\u2019s tempting to give him <b>Increasing Strength Exercise</b> to represent his fantastic feats, but he really doesn\u2019t need that: in the books, he never demonstrates anything that cannot be accomplished with Strength 5. Just give him Strength 5, Athletics 5, a specialty in Feats of Strength, and three dots in the Mighty Thew Merit. Now with stunting (and Conan always stunts), he is tossing sixteen dice at Feats of Strength. Add in a point of Willpower, aim for a level 2 stunt, and he can manage even a Difficulty 10 Strength 5 Feat in a pinch.<br /> <br /> What about actual combat? Conan has no problem dealing with large groups of foes. This is easily explained: battle groups! The most surprising thing here is that Conan\u2019s quickness is often more important than his strength or resilience. In single combat, he typically draws his weapon and lands a killing blow right out the gate, which is best represented by possessing a brutal Join Battle roll. Perception 5, Awareness 5, with a Join Battle specialty and Fast Reflexes will take him pretty far (especially if supplemented with a point of Willpower). If you\u2019re on the edge, then giving him an Awareness Excellency is enough to widen the gap against mere mortals.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say Conan is Supernal Resistance. You can duplicate most of his enduring prowess by giving him pretty much every Merit that has Stamina or Resistance as a prerequisite. Set his Stamina and Resistance both to five, and he\u2019ll clear most of the obstacles listed in the book. However, there are occasions where I feel Conan <i>must </i>be pushed past mortal endurance. The stand-out moment is in one story where Conan is beaten up by a group of soldiers, then crucified. He still possesses the strength, after two days in the sun, to kill a vulture with his teeth, survive falling face-forward onto the ground with the weight of the crucifix behind him, yank out two of his own crucifix nails, and then ride ten miles unassisted without water. If a person can survive all of that and recover after only a few days, they\u2019re beyond mortal.<br /> <br /> How <i>deep </i>Conan needs to go into the Resistance tree is a different question. I\u2019m sure he possesses <b>Armored Scout\u2019s Invigoration </b>(his stealthiness in armor is a key trait) and \u2013 coming back around to combat \u2013 I expect he draws upon<b> Battle Fury Focus</b>, or even<b> Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit</b>, when faced with supernatural threats and endless hordes of foes. His ability to parry with a sword is impressive (and he might possess <b>Dipping Swallow Defense</b>), but it\u2019s really his ability to withstand blows and keep going that stands out: I\u2019d give him maxed out <b>Ox-Body Technique</b> for sure, and he likely possesses a few other Resistance Charms beside. If you're this deep into Resistance, you might take a few others to round it out, but Stamina/Resistance Merits accomplish much the same thing. It's really his ability to <i>not die</i> from repeated injuries that is the focus here.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s a few other points of note.<br /> <br /> Conan might possess <b>Sensory Acuity Prana</b>: he has almost preternatural hearing and sight. His abilities never get to the point where it seems downright impossible, but it definitely resides on the border of possibility.<br /> <br /> Stealth is another key Ability. Conan can move silently at a full run, and it\u2019s tempting to say he possesses a Charm which removes any bonus that enemies might get for listening to him moving. His opponents rarely hear him coming, and surprise attacks are fairly common.<br /> <br /> He possesses dots in most Abilities, but here\u2019s some notable ones. His War ability is rated at least at four dots. He has Larceny, but you know that already. Brawl and Melee are his highest-rated Abilities; both are likely at 5. Give him a dot in Occult to represent his knowledge of the supernatural and (though he loathes it) a couple dots in Bureaucracy; he\u2019s accustomed to haggling with merchants and, later in life, he makes for a good king. His social stats (Attributes and Abilities) are all pretty decent all around, and he\u2019s often drawing upon Intimacies of fear or awe toward himself to weaken his target\u2019s Resolve. He possesses Linguistics, and is talented enough that his style is as unmistakable as it is bold. He also speaks a variety of languages, including ancient and dead tongues.<br /> <br /> <b>Do not forget Lore</b>. Conan must possess Lore at 3+. In most of his adventures, he establishes at least one fact relating to cultural practices, religion, politics, geography, or history. His ability to both establish facts and contradict others is a key facet of his character, providing him with the upper hand against his opponents, and guidance in dangerous situations.<br /> <br /> Conan\u2019s social Merits vary over time and fluctuate wildly. Sometimes he\u2019s a penniless vagabond. Other times he has commanded hundreds of men for a warlord. And, at one time, he was a king. The only thing which remains stable is his Influence, which grows over time. Later in his career, Conan becomes a figure of awe and a legend even in his own time.<br /> <br /> On a final note, he possesses a minor Intimacy of fear toward Sorcery. It\u2019s strong enough that he will avoid dealing with sorcerers if reasonably possible, but other concerns often override it. He certainly won\u2019t stay behind to finish off a sorcerer if he\u2019s got what he\u2019s come for.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, here\u2019s what we have\u2026<br /> Conan is the perfect example of a Solar whose essence-enhanced prowess is just subtle enough that mortals don\u2019t question it. Conan <i>might be </i>a Heroic Mortal who possesses maxed out stats in several Attributes and Abilities, along with armloads of Merits, whose regularly doubling the pools of his rivals. However, he most likely <i>is </i>a Dawn Caste Solar, with Supernal Resistance, but a relatively light Charm investment. When pressed to mortal limits, he draws upon Excellencies from his Favored Abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","user":"Fetch","date":". 09-12-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:18:52-07:00","id":968136,"title":"","content":"looks fair enough<br /> <br /> he should have a positive intimacy for wenches and ale","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:01:04-07:00","id":968161,"title":"","content":"Incidentally I would love to just make, like, Conan in Creation. The exact same character, really, from the exact same kind of tribe, gets a Solar Exaltation. What kind is he? What are his charms? Supernal Resistance or Athletics seem right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:51:39-07:00","id":968323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968161#post968161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally I would love to just make, like, Conan in Creation. The exact same character, really, from the exact same kind of tribe, gets a Solar Exaltation. What kind is he? What are his charms? Supernal Resistance or Athletics seem right to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You basically take what I mentioned above and transplant it into Creation unmodified. The world of Exalted maps closely to Conan's, and that's not accidental.<br /> <br /> Conan has impressive Athletics (again, I suggest Athletics 5), but he doesn't need to go Supernal Athletics, and he does just fine without any Athletics Charms. The only Athletics path he might take are Charms which increase his Strength, but it's unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Now if you wanted an &quot;amped up&quot; Conan, i.e. taking Conan's natural talents and amplifying them to heroic anime levels, then you might give him all sorts of Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:29:39-07:00","id":968355,"title":"","content":"Crom is another name for the Unconquered Sun, they've just only worshiped him in the time when he has turned his face from Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/246-wretch","name":"Wretch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:48:42-07:00","id":968383,"title":"","content":"Of course, if you take <i>comic book</i> Conan into account, then there is no arguing he might just be a &quot;maxed out&quot; mortal. Waaaay too many superhuman feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:27:43-07:00","id":968460,"title":"","content":"I'd also argue that he has at least a fair Archery - he pulls off a handful of impressive feats with a bow. He's also no stranger to Thrown, considering he killed a man with a thrown stool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:47:42-07:00","id":968467,"title":"","content":"I don't know; I'd honestly say that Conan is just a Heroic Mortal. You have to remember that for mortals, 2 is considered &quot;average&quot; for an Attribute and &quot;professionally trained&quot; for a Skill. Most mortals won't have traits that exceed 2 or dice pools that exceed 5. Conan's ratings of 5 in all Physical Attributes and remarkably high ratings in Social and Mental Attributes are already putting him on par or just about with your average professionally trained human being. Then you add his own Skill ratings and he's leaving them high and dry, outclassing them in nearly every category you can care to imagine. He's very much an exceptional mortal, but he's not going to be chucking elephants or nearly flying any time soon. He's putting all of his Experience into his Traits and Willpower instead of Charms.<br /> <br /> If he's any kind of Exalt, he's probably an Exigent of Crom. In 2e, Crom was another name for the Unconquered Sun, but that may not be true in 3e, or he may be a minor aspect god of the UC focused on physical prowess. I can imagine him to be a minor War God with a focused purview on physical prowess, and thus his Exigent would have subtle powers of physical superiority. That his Exigent is also pretty darn smart and sociable is just a happy bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:00:45-07:00","id":968547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968460#post968460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also argue that he has at least a fair Archery - he pulls off a handful of impressive feats with a bow. He's also no stranger to Thrown, considering he killed a man with a thrown stool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, definitely. I lost that point somewhere in my editing. <br /> <br /> You should assume Conan has Archery and Thrown rated at least at 3 dots. There's a point in one of stories where he is middle-aged and he comments that - when he was younger - he could knock a bird out of the sky with a well-thrown stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:46:19-07:00","id":968617,"title":"","content":"Conan isn't showing Exalted levels of capability, but in his world, Exaltations don't exist. If Not!Conan existed in Creation, he'd make for an excellent Exalted character of various stripes. Probably a Solar, potentially a Lunar though. Anyway, if he was, I think he'd be mostly getting charms related to combat and feats of endurance and athleticism, as well as a few larceny, stealth and survival charms to help him get by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:24:20-07:00","id":968677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968136#post968136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">looks fair enough<br /> <br /> he should have a positive intimacy for wenches and ale</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much the original Robert E. Howard Conan, which Sword Emperor is talking about. You're talking about the exagerrated, Flanderized pop-culture Conan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:43:05-07:00","id":968686,"title":"","content":"I'd put a point or two into sail. The guy was a pirate for a few years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:07:03-07:00","id":968727,"title":"","content":"Howard's Conan probably has a few dots in pretty much every Ability by the time he's on Aquilonia's throne, but I'm definitely not seeing him at Exalted level of capabilities. If he really must be, I'd go with Solar up there and say he's a low to medium-powered Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:17:01-07:00","id":968814,"title":"","content":"Here is an expression of Conan's Intimacies, Limit Trigger, and Limit Break, in accordance with Robert E Howard's work, adjusted to fit within the context of Creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Minor: </b>Sorcery (Fear)<br /> <b>Defining: </b>Civilization corrupts and weakens<br /> <b>Minor: </b>Homeland (Affection)<br /> <b>Defining: </b>Better a peaceful king than a tyrannical emperor<br /> <b>Major: </b>I will not leave anyone - friend or foe - to the mercies of monsters<br /> <b>Defining: </b>I will never betray afriend or companion<br /> <b>Minor: </b>I must accept that glory and wealth are fleeting<br /> <b>Defining: </b>The fine arts must be glorified and preserved<br /> <b>Defining:</b> Seek the affections of beautiful companions<br /> <b>Minor: </b>I must be honorable in my dealings<br /> <b>Minor: </b>I owe neither honesty or loyalty to betrayers<br /> <b>Major: </b>If I am a stronger leader than my liege, I must replace him<br /> <b>Minor: </b>Deception and stealth are the preferred approach against a foe or rival<br /> <b>Minor: </b>When you don't know what to do, rush the enemy<br /> <b>Defining: </b>Violence is a good solution<br /> <b>Major: </b>Live a wanderer's life<br /> <b>Minor: </b>Worship is pointless<br /> <b>Major: </b>Seek wealth and personal gain<br /> <b>Defining: </b>Experience all the wonders of life<br /> <br /> <b>Limit Trigger: </b>Failure to protect a friend or companion, whether by action or inaction<br /> <b>Limit Break: </b>Seek vengeance against whomever or whatever caused the harm. Conan will take a strategic advantage if one is available, but he will abandon all other concerns - even personal safety - to mete vengeance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:18:49-07:00","id":968843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968727#post968727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Howard's Conan probably has a few dots in pretty much every Ability by the time he's on Aquilonia's throne, but I'm definitely not seeing him at Exalted level of capabilities. If he really must be, I'd go with Solar up there and say he's a low to medium-powered Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether Conan is Exalted is... questionable. Most of his prowess falls on the upper end of the human spectrum, but his endurance may be off the charts. The crucifixion in <b>A Witch Shall be Born </b>is the clearest indication that Conan possesses superhuman resilience (read the details in my post above). You might also have a look at the bear trap from <b>Red Nails</b>, which has the following choice passage.<br /> &quot;The jaws of an iron trap had closed on his leg, with teeth that sank deep and held. Only the ridged muscles on his calf saved the bone from bei<br /> <br /> I'm not well versed enough on human anatomy to state definitively either way, but any argument should factor in those two passages before passing judgment.<br /> <br /> As for what <i>type </i>of Exalted (supposing he is), I would still go with Solar. Solars are the archetypical heroes, whose feats of prowess are all extensions of mortal ability. Conan definitely fits that mold, and he's a poster boy for modeling a Dawn Caste (whether or not he is Exalted).<br /> <br /> I'm wary of electing him to the ranks of Exigents. I tend to think of the Exigents as purpose-driven in a way that doesn't correspond well with REH's Conan.<br /> <br /> So, all that said, if someone just said &quot;Conan is a mortal with maxed out stats in several Attributes and Abilities&quot;, I wouldn't put up a big argument. He definitely hovers on the edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:46:47-07:00","id":968862,"title":"","content":"In <i>Xuthal of the Dusk</i>, he also takes a fall that, while the exact height isn't given, would definitely have killed a lesser man. After being pushed to his limits wandering the desert. And then he goes on to fight an amorphous monster. And despite being lacerated nearly to ribbons by it, survives long enough to be administered healing.<br /> <br /> Really, one of the biggest indicators of Exalted hardiness on his part is that he's still <i>fit</i> to fight by the time he sits the throne of Aquilonia. A mortal fighter not only wouldn't survive the abuses Conan routinely endures, he would probably be crippled for life by <i>one</i> such adventure.<br /> <br /> (Side story: Someone I know loves bowling. He even bowled himself, and managed a couple of 300 games. About ten years ago, he fell the space of ten feet on the job, and landed on his right shoulder, and now he can no longer raise that arm above that shoulder. Needless to say, he hasn't done much bowling since.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:11:52-07:00","id":968875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968814#post968814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Minor: </b>Homeland (Affection)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I think you are more like them than you are like your own race,\u201d laughed Prospero. \u201cYou laugh greatly, drink deep and bellow good songs, whereas I never saw another Cimmerian who drank aught but water, or who ever laughed, or ever sang save to chant dismal dirges.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps it\u2019s the land they live in,\u201d answered Conan. \u201cA gloomier land never existed on earth. It is all of hills, heavily wooded, and the trees are strangely dusky, so that even by day all the land looks dark and menacing. As far as a man may see his eye rests on the endless vistas of hills beyond hills, growing darker and darker in the distance. Clouds hang always among those hills; the skies are nearly always gray. Winds blow sharp and cold, driving rain or sleet or snow before them, and moan drearily among the passes and down the valleys. There is little mirth in that land.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cLittle wonder men grow moody there,\u201d quoth Prospero with a shrug of his shoulders, thinking of the smiling sun-washed plains and blue lazy rivers of Poitain, Aquilonia\u2019s southern-most province.<br /> <br /> \u201cStrange and moody, indeed,\u201d answered Conan. \u201cLife seems bitter and hard and futile. The men of those dark hills brood overmuch on unknown things. They dream monstrous dreams. Their gods are Crom and his dark race, and they believe the world of the dead is a cold, sunless place of everlasting mist, where wandering ghosts go wailing forevermore. They have no hope here or hereafter, and they brood too much on the emptiness of life. I have seen the strange madness of futility fall upon them when a little thing like a spinning dust-cloud, or the hollow crying of a bird, or the moan of the wind through bare branches brought to their gloomy minds the emptiness of life and the vainness of existence. Only in war are the Cimmerians happy. Mitra! The ways of the \u00c6sir were more to my liking.\u201d......<br /> <br /> His gusty laughter followed Prospero out of the chamber. The carven door closed behind the Poitanian, and Conan turned back to his task. He paused a moment, idly listening to his friend\u2019s retreating footsteps, which fell hollowly on the tiles. And as if the empty sound struck a kindred chord in his soul, a rush of revulsion swept over him. His mirth fell away from him like a mask, and his face was suddenly old, his eyes worn. The unreasoning melancholy of the Cimmerian fell like a shroud about his soul, paralyzing him with a crushing sense of the futility of human endeavor and the meaninglessness of life. His kingship, his pleasures, his fears, his ambitions, and all earthly things were revealed to him suddenly as dust and broken toys. The borders of life shrivelled and the lines of existence closed in about him, numbing him. Dropping his lion head in his mighty hands, he groaned aloud.<br /> <br /> Then lifting his head, as a man looks for escape, his eyes fell on a crystal jar of yellow wine. Quickly he rose and pouring a goblet full, quaffed it at a gulp. Again he filled and emptied the goblet, and again. When he set it down, a fine warmth stole through his veins. Things and happenings assumed new values. The dark Cimmerian hills faded far behind him. Life was good and real and vibrant after all \u2013 not the dream of an idiot god. He stretched himself lazily like a gigantic cat and seated himself at the table, conscious of the magnitude and vital importance of himself and his task. Contentedly, he nibbled his stylus and eyed his map.<br /> <br /> - &quot;The Phoenix on the Sword,&quot; first submitted draft<br /> <br /> TLDR version: I'd say that he is actually afraid of his homeland more than anything else. Just talking about it seems to throw him into an existential crisis. And yes, I know I should have shortened it more but I love Howard's writing style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:31:28-07:00","id":968892,"title":"","content":"You can make a pretty solid argument for Howard's original Conan being flat-out clinically depressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:47:52-07:00","id":968907,"title":"","content":"Well. Ghost.<br /> <br /> That's a good point. I rescind my statement!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:47:14-07:00","id":968937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968843#post968843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whether Conan is Exalted is... questionable. Most of his prowess falls on the upper end of the human spectrum, but his endurance may be off the charts. The crucifixion in <b>A Witch Shall be Born </b>is the clearest indication that Conan possesses superhuman resilience (read the details in my post above). You might also have a look at the bear trap from <b>Red Nails</b>, which has the following choice passage.<br /> &quot;The jaws of an iron trap had closed on his leg, with teeth that sank deep and held. Only the ridged muscles on his calf saved the bone from bei<br /> <br /> I'm not well versed enough on human anatomy to state definitively either way, but any argument should factor in those two passages before passing judgment.<br /> <br /> As for what <i>type </i>of Exalted (supposing he is), I would still go with Solar. Solars are the archetypical heroes, whose feats of prowess are all extensions of mortal ability. Conan definitely fits that mold, and he's a poster boy for modeling a Dawn Caste (whether or not he is Exalted).<br /> <br /> I'm wary of electing him to the ranks of Exigents. I tend to think of the Exigents as purpose-driven in a way that doesn't correspond well with REH's Conan.<br /> <br /> So, all that said, if someone just said &quot;Conan is a mortal with maxed out stats in several Attributes and Abilities&quot;, I wouldn't put up a big argument. He definitely hovers on the edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there's this fuzzy area between &quot;Newly Exalted Solar&quot; and &quot;Jacked up Heroic Mortal with 5s in everything and 30 dots of merits and stuff&quot; where you could argue either way about people.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I were trying to translate Conan over as a Solar, I'd put his attributes and ability ratings at a bit less than what might be indicated from the books and make sure he had excellencies in all the main areas. Because Conan doesn't have to have superhuman prowess all the time and adding excellency dice will allow him to pull off those big rolls when he needs to.<br /> <br /> Another thing to remember about translating other fictional characters into Exalted is that, narratively speaking, the Exaltation is Creation's equivalent of the &quot;cinematic pulp action rules&quot; or whatever that makes that person a Bad-Ass. So, Sherlock Holmes, Conan, and Batman would all be Exalted in Creation, because that's how the game is designed, in much the same way they'd all be Inspired if you were playing Adventure or have High Tier Strange Skills if you were playing FATE Kerberos Club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:47:17-07:00","id":968939,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing about Conan is that he likes civilization. He just hates what civilization does to people. They inevitably become amoral, corrupt, indolent... and evil. <b>Exalted</b>'s setting reflects this viewpoints. The decadent corruption of every Creation-spanning empire reflects the decayed cultures depicted in <b>Xuthal of the Dusk </b>and <b>Red Nails. </b>A land which becomes too civilized ultimately devours itself. Whether this is better than the alternative - reverting to barbarianism - is an interesting question that Conan struggles with. Conan's life as king is one of the most interesting aspects of his character, because it reflects a central question of the Solars: not whether they have power, but whether they should exercise it. He makes himself a king, but it forces him to civilize himself. The corruption never quite touches him in the stories, but it infects his followers (as best seen in <b>The Phoenix on the Sword</b>), and he forever faces the temptation to abandon his responsibilities. Howard never wrote an ending to Conan's life, but speculated that he was ultimately forced into a war of conquest for self-defense, and may (or may not) have died in one of the conflicts.<br /> <br /> I recommend using this as insight into adventures for Solar heroes who becomes rulers. You may slay the cruel satrap and his puppet king, then take their place, but who do you put in place of their cronies? How do you handle insubordination from the people you are trying to protect? When you hear the call to adventure, who sits upon your throne (remembering that Conan had no heir, which caused its own problems during a rebellion)? How do you deal with well-intentioned traitors? How do you punish people who have become corrupt only because of your largesse? And who do you trust during a revolt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:58:06-07:00","id":968946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968892#post968892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can make a pretty solid argument for Howard's original Conan being flat-out clinically depressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the similarities between Conan and his author (both were six-foot white guys who punched people and didn't think too highly of civilization), it's not too surprising, considering Howard killed himself at the age of 30.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:09:09-07:00","id":969019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=968946#post968946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the similarities between Conan and his author (both were six-foot white guys who punched people and didn't think too highly of civilization), it's not too surprising, considering Howard killed himself at the age of 30.</div> </div> </div> </div>Howard is a character is the Conan stories actually. He dies off screen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> My very basic research into Howard makes me think that the &quot;didn't think too highly of civilization&quot; is probably not very accurate. If I remember correctly it was more along the lines that Howard thought that civilization was temporary. It would crash eventually and then we would be savages, and then we would have a civilization, then it would crash, etc, etc, etc. I seem to remember that he had a lot of choice words about people who thought there was something noble about being a barbarian. Its a real shame to American Literature that the guy just had to know what a gun barrel tasted like. (I personally think that if he survived and was allowed to branch out then we may not of had almost 50 years of fantasy literature basically defined as &quot;It's like Tolkien, but...&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","user":"Ghost","date":". 09-14-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:09:48-07:00","id":969062,"title":"","content":"I generally don't consider &quot;temporary, destined to come crashing down into barbarism&quot; to be high praise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T01:10:07-07:00","id":969081,"title":"","content":"Conan is a Solar, just not a particularly powerful one. If he were a player character, he'd be played by the guy who doesn't quite buy into the animesque aesthetics of some higher Essence Solar Charms, and thus prefers to keep to the lower-Essence ones, dipping into multiple Abilities instead of specializing in just a couple.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all Solar abilities begin this way - with feats of supreme, but not blatantly supernatural prowess. Conan is one of the fictional characters whose exploits define this lower level of Solar power, alongside such staples as Sherlock Holmes or Batman. To say he's not a Solar because he doesn't exhibit those flashier, higher-powered abilities some Solars have is missing the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T02:57:01-07:00","id":969113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=969081#post969081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conan is a Solar, just not a particularly powerful one. If he were a player character, he'd be played by the guy who doesn't quite buy into the animesque aesthetics of some higher Essence Solar Charms, and thus prefers to keep to the lower-Essence ones, dipping into multiple Abilities instead of specializing in just a couple.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all Solar abilities begin this way - with feats of supreme, but not blatantly supernatural prowess. Conan is one of the fictional characters whose exploits define this lower level of Solar power, alongside such staples as Sherlock Holmes or Batman. To say he's not a Solar because he doesn't exhibit those flashier, higher-powered abilities some Solars have is missing the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this. Supernal Resistance Dawn Caste Solar whose spread himself through most of the Abilities on the list rather than taking any of the Essence 4 or 5 abilities, making him supernaturally competent at pretty much everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:18:44-07:00","id":969155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=969062#post969062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't consider &quot;temporary, destined to come crashing down into barbarism&quot; to be high praise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be high praise, but I think there's a gradient worth taking note of between &quot;Civilization is an Objectively Bad Thing that makes men weak and thus should be discarded and destroyed as a moral imperative&quot; - 1e Lunars, &quot;Ideological Barbarians&quot; as<a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\"> Holden puts it,</a> etc - and stuff like &quot;Civilization is nice while it stays civilized, but men eventually become barbaric to each other even while dressed in fine silks and drinking rich wines&quot; - as the Sword Emperor elaborates on the Conan story.<br /> <br /> One is saying that people of various identities living together without a master-subject or pillager-pillaged relationship is a bad thing in and of itself and no utopia can be unless we wipe with poison ivy leaves and wonder why we itch, the other that such a thing is going to be inherently threatened by the would-be masters and pillagers seeking to tear it apart so they can elevate themselves in some way, in a way that will probably end in revolution and fire..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 09-14-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:59:39-07:00","id":969291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=969062#post969062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't consider &quot;temporary, destined to come crashing down into barbarism&quot; to be high praise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Count, I don't know how to tell you this, but I have some bad news about this whole &quot;life&quot; thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:31:41-07:00","id":969306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=969062#post969062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't consider &quot;temporary, destined to come crashing down into barbarism&quot; to be high praise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it was meant to be praise or criticism. By my (very basic) reading of his work, it was more of an observation. This is going off of memory, but he seemed to view European/North African history as cycling between civilization and barbarism with the barbarism part holding his personal interest. If I remember right, examples that he pointed out on the barbarism parts is the European Dark Ages and the American frontier pioneers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:45:44-07:00","id":969312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=969291#post969291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Count, I don't know how to tell you this, but I have some bad news about this whole &quot;life&quot; thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly feel like giving a sarcastic-asshole reply, so\u2026<br /> <br /> Yeah, life ends, as can a civilization. <b>Making the observation that it ends is not, in and of itself, praise.</b> It <i>can</i> be, but it's really hard to squeeze in how good it is when you're also conveying a message of how pointless existence is and how we're propping ourselves up on lies about how important we are to justify the things that we do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:11:25-07:00","id":969329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/968127-conan-the-solar?p=969312#post969312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't particularly feel like giving a sarcastic-asshole reply, so\u2026<br /> <br /> Yeah, life ends, as can a civilization. <b>Making the observation that it ends is not, in and of itself, praise.</b> It <i>can</i> be, but it's really hard to squeeze in how good it is when you're also conveying a message of how pointless existence is and how we're propping ourselves up on lies about how important we are to justify the things that we do.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant to say is that if we can only value things by their permanence, then nothing can ever have value, which makes permanence unhelpful as a metric of worth. I believe that it's more useful, especially in the context of Exalted, to discuss how the very forces that drive progress and civilization can, in different contexts and under different constraints, tear those very things asunder, and how if even the greatest and most-glorious things and people can and will eventually fall to corruption and entropy, perhaps one should consider this before doing ghastly things to others under the pretext that their lives mean less than one's own. Yes, you may have a literal, no-shit divine mandate to do as you please with the world, but please remember that the gods of Creation are <i>assholes.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}